    },
    {
      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "content": "<p>This quiet seasonal scene by Xugu pairs lively myna birds—starlings native to Asia—with chrysanthemums. The flowers, which bloom in late autumn, symbolize longevity and resilience. Myna birds, admired for their intelligence and animated presence, convey harmonious social exchange based on integrity and honesty. After a career as a military officer, Xugu became a Buddhist monk-painter. He was celebrated for revitalizing birdand-flower painting with his highly unorthodox style. Executed with brisk, calligraphic brushwork and subtle tonal variations, this scroll exemplifies his ability to balance disciplined structure with bursts of spontaneity. His  abbreviated forms and expressive ink handling lend an air of vitality to this reflective moment.</p>\n",
      "classified_as": [
